# Local development.
#
# The public site connects READ-ONLY through this URL and relies on row-level
# security for isolation, so pointing it at a database with other tenants in it
# is safe by design. It is still a local database only.
# Port 5433, not 5432: a pre-existing PostgreSQL service on the host commonly
# holds 5432, and the connection silently goes there instead of to Docker.
#   docker run -d --name forecourt-db -e POSTGRES_PASSWORD=postgres \
#     -e POSTGRES_DB=forecourt -p 5433:5432 postgres:16
DATABASE_URL=postgres://postgres:postgres@localhost:5433/forecourt

# Optional. Renders the finance block locally against a DEMO compliance
# sign-off. Never set this anywhere a customer can reach.
# DEMO_SIGN_COMPLIANCE_RULE=1

# TEMPORARY. Lets an operator into apps/admin with a password alone.
#
# The admin application requires a second factor for every screen, but the
# enrolment and challenge screens do not exist yet, so without this a correct
# password produces a session that is immediately bounced back to sign-in. It
# is the only way in until those screens are built.
#
# Understand what it costs before setting it in a deployment: admin reads
# across every dealership on the platform, so this makes one password the
# whole protection on all of them. It shows a banner on every page while it is
# on. Remove it, and the bypass in apps/admin/src/auth/session.ts, as soon as
# enrolment ships.
# ADMIN_MFA_BYPASS=1

# Vehicle and logo photographs.
#
# Locally, leave these unset. Bytes land in `.media/` under the process cwd.
#
# On Railway, set the four R2_* variables on BOTH crm and site (same values).
# Railway cannot share one volume between two services, so a disk on each
# is two empty folders. R2 is the shared store. Do not set these on admin.
#
# Create the bucket in the EU jurisdiction (UK dealer photographs, some of
# them taken at a customer's house). Then:
#
#   R2_ACCOUNT_ID=            Cloudflare account id
#   R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID=         S3 API token — Access Key ID
#   R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=     S3 API token — Secret Access Key
#   R2_BUCKET=rixdrive-media
#   R2_JURISDICTION=eu
#
# Optional override if the default host is wrong:
#   R2_ENDPOINT=https://<ACCOUNT_ID>.eu.r2.cloudflarestorage.com
#
# The bucket stays PRIVATE. Unpublished and part-exchange photographs must
# not be world-readable. The apps serve through /media after a tenant check.
#
# MEDIA_LOCAL_ROOT is the disk fallback when R2 is unset (local, or a single
# service with a Railway volume). It is ignored once R2 is fully configured.
# MEDIA_LOCAL_ROOT=/var/media

# The dev server's port. `next dev` reads this from the real environment, not
# from this file, so to change it for one run:
#   PowerShell:  $env:PORT=3001; pnpm dev
#   bash/zsh:    PORT=3001 pnpm dev
# PORT=3000

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- deployment
#
# Nothing below belongs in a local .env — it is here so the deployment's
# variables are documented in the same place as the local ones.
#
# On Railway each service needs exactly two:
#
#   APP=crm | site | admin       selects which app the shared Dockerfile builds
#   DATABASE_URL=${{Postgres.DATABASE_URL}}
#                                a REFERENCE to the database service, so it
#                                follows the database if it moves
#
# Do NOT set PORT — Railway injects it and the standalone server reads it.
#
# To run migrations from your machine, use Railway's PUBLIC url and add
# sslmode, because the proxy's certificate is not in Node's trust store:
#
#   DATABASE_URL='postgresql://...@turntable.proxy.rlwy.net:PORT/railway?sslmode=require' \
#     pnpm db:deploy
#
# See docs/12-deploying-to-railway.md.
